    "done_when": "Start from the qualifying weak-110 receipt driver at docs/figures/centroid-constrained-oracle-solve/repaired-remeasure-receipt/measure.py (global 2.68e-14, row 9.53e-15 pitches against the derived tolerance 1.66e-4, net span -3.86e-4). A committed driver under docs/figures/centroid-constrained-oracle-solve/certificate-ladder-110-300/ runs as ONE H200 job (betelgeuse, reservation gpu_0003_grpA, one card, 8 CPUs, --mem=128G, --time=02:00:00, TMPDIR=/tmp in submit and payload, the shared interpreter /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/nova/.venv/bin/python without uv, submitted with RECKON_ALLOW_NESTED_LAUNCH=1 sbatch, never srun or salloc; submit for real and read squeue after a minute, and only if it is still PENDING on a resource or configuration reason resubmit to titan with --partition=titan --gres=gpu:1 and say so). Inside it, the rows weak-rotation-reactor-static, moderate-rotation-conventional-static and strong-rotation-compact-static at requested cells -110 and -300 are solved sequentially with clip_mode=exact passed explicitly, from the production seed, with the first-moment centroid row imposed, and each row receipt is persisted as it lands so an expiry loses one row. Each row records: max solved-minus-analytic over span against ten times 1.1e-4, magnetic-axis error in pitches against 0.1, boundary level offset over span against 1e-3, the compensating field amplitudes, the terminal global residual and the row residual (each against 1e-12) plus the row residual in pitches against its derived tolerance, the realised cell count, and compile seconds separated from solve seconds. The same rows under the whole-cell support are re-solved under the same row as the negative control and must show the centroid moved to the oracle while the roughly 0.2-of-span booking error remains; the plan section 3 names this control, and where the certificate driver keeps its whole-cell rows is for you to find. Per row, a line-contour panel shows solved over analytic on shared physical levels and the difference, with both null sets, the wall, and the terminal residual and converged flag in the caption. The report /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/nova/s22/cco-certificate-ladder-110-300.md tables every row with pass or fail per clause and states whether the compensating amplitude falls from 110 to 300 cells; the fragment docs/evidence/fragments/centroid-constrained-oracle-solve/cco-certificate-ladder-110-300.html carries the table and panels with project-absolute src. A row that fails a clause is reported as measured, never tuned; no source under nova/ is edited. Keep scratch under the run directory, not /tmp, which is at 91 percent on the fleet node. The job runs longer than your turn budget: once it is admitted, commit, write status waiting with the sacct probe as wait_probe and the job id in wait_condition, and end the turn; the recovery sweep resumes you when the job is terminal, and that resumed turn reads the receipts, renders the panels and writes the report. This gate measures only this node; a failure outside its scope goes under follow_ons.",
